## Publication settings

The root settings below make our current defaults explicit. The theme applies to
preview, HTML and LaTeX; font selection currently applies only to LaTeX books.
Change any font family independently: `font-body` selects prose, `font-heading`
selects headings, `font-code` selects code, `font-fragment` selects fragment
names and references, and `font-note` selects running matter and reference page
numbers. Omit `font-note` to inherit `font-body`; specifying it fixes that role
independently. Use `font-code-ligatures=off` to disable contextual code ligatures.

Font values are family names, not file paths. Selecting a family does not install
it: make it available to the TeX compiler, or explicitly provide its faces and
licenses with the CLI's `--font-manifest` option. Chapter-local settings do not
override these root font choices. See [Publication font settings](literate/publication-settings.html)
and [Portable font companions](literate/publication-fonts.html) for details.

``` SETTINGS
authors=Nathan 'jesterKing' Letwory
theme=rosepine-dawn
font-body=Latin Modern Roman
font-heading=Monofur Nerd Font
font-code=Lilex Nerd Font
font-fragment=Monofur Nerd Font
font-note=Latin Modern Roman
font-code-ligatures=on
```
